- Accept an application-supplied mailbox key through `WalletSeed`.
  Persist its full public identity and network, and refuse reopening with a
  missing or different key. The application retains responsibility for backup.
  [#3](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/3)
  - **BREAKING:** `WalletProperties` requires `mailbox_identity`; the default
    mailbox uses BIP86 external index zero. Registration-shaped stores are refused.
- Track explicit fallback receipts and their stage-selected source aliases.
  Paid receipts require six canonical confirmations; reorgs restore pending
  principal without inventing a Lightning outcome or duplicate movement.
  [#3](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/3)
  - **BREAKING:** Registration, `fallback_spk` and the inferred fallback snapshot
    API are removed; use `fallback_script` and `fallback_receipts`.
- Keep a transfer refused for fallback separate from successful delivery.
  Exact input-owner receipts preserve the signed checkpoint until canonical
  retirement, without adding a second successful debit to payment history.
  [#3](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/3)
